// ─── INTRO (FIRST-TERM) PRICE ON A CUSTOM BUILD (2026-09-29) ────────────────
// The live catalog sells every VPS plan and almost every game tier with a lower
// FIRST-term price that renews at the regular `priceCents` (`Plan.introPriceCents` /
// `GamePlan.introPriceCents`, `introTermMonths: null` = the whole first term, any
// length). Read from prod 2026-09-29: all 4 active VPS plans and 120 of 135 active
// game tiers carry one at 69.44%-69.53% of `priceCents` (roughly 30.5% off). Custom
// builds carried none, so a custom order's first charge was its full renewal price.
//
// A custom row now gets `introPriceCents = round(priceCents × (100 − pct) / 100)`, pct
// being the admin setting `custom_plan_intro_percent` (default 30), and
// `introTermMonths: null`. That is ALL the new money logic there is: lib/order.ts
// `orderQuote` and lib/game-order.ts `gameOrderQuote` already apply any row's intro
// price to its first term and stamp `Server.termPromoPercent`, and renewal
// (lib/renewal-charge.ts) never reads the intro columns, so it still bills the
// regular price (frozen on `Server.grandfatheredRenewalCents`).
//
// Two guards keep it in line with the catalog it extends:
//   1. INHERITED, NOT BLANKET. A custom build gets an intro price only if the plan it
//      extends does: VPS Max for a VPS build, the family's own top real tier for a
//      game build (`anchorIntroCents` null means no intro). Five game families
//      (armareforger, ats, cs16, dayz, ets2) sell every tier at the regular price.
//      A 30%-off custom build there would sell its first term BELOW that family's top
//      premade tier, even though it is strictly bigger. If the owner adds intro prices
//      to those tiers, their custom builds pick one up with no code change.
//   2. ANTI-UNDERCUT. The same invariant `computeCustomPlanPriceCents` enforces on
//      the regular price, applied to the first term: a custom intro never prices
//      at or below the anchor's own intro price. At the default 30% this can't bind
//      (custom price > anchor price, and 0.70 > every live anchor's ~0.695 ratio).
//      It only matters if an admin raises the percent far enough to invert them.
export const CUSTOM_PLAN_DEFAULT_INTRO_PERCENT = 30;

/** The intro terms a custom build inherits. `null` = sold at the regular price
 *  from day one (the anchor has no intro price, or the setting is 0). */
export type CustomPlanIntro = {
