// ANTI-UNDERCUT, the same invariant `computeCustomPlanPriceCents` /
// `computeCustomGamePlanPriceCents` enforce on the regular price, applied to the
// first term. A custom build is strictly bigger than the plan it extends (VPS Max,
// or the game family's own top tier), so its first term must never cost less than
// THAT plan's first term. That is its intro price, or its regular price if it has
// none. The clamp binds in exactly one place in prod today: `armareforger`, one of
// five families (armareforger, ats, cs16, dayz, ets2) whose tiers carry no intro
